# Backend configuration lives in the repository-root .env.example.
#
# Settings are loaded from `.env` then `../.env` (see app/core/config.py), so
# running the API from this directory picks up the root file either way. Copy
# that one:
#
#     cp ../.env.example ../.env
#
# Every variable is documented in docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
#
# This file previously listed AWS access keys, a Redis URL, Sentry DSNs and a
# dozen feature flags belonging to an earlier version of this project. None of
# them were read by any code, ENVIRONMENT=development was not a valid value,
# and CORS_ORIGINS carried a wildcard that Starlette cannot parse — copying it
# to .env stopped the application from starting.
